<title>USA: Beaufort County, S.C., defeats roads tax.</title>
<headline>Beaufort County, S.C., defeats roads tax.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLESTON, S. C. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Residents of Beaufort County roundly defeated a once cent sales tax hike that was slated for highway improvements, an official in the county voter registration office said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The measure drew 21,490 no votes and 10,482 yes votes, according to the county official.</p>
<p>The money would have been used to improve a section of highway linking Beaufort and Hilton Head Island where 19 people have died in the past three years, local press reports said.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
